---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Mission and editorial principles of The Independent Observer."
  currentPath="/about/"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About the project"
    title="Independence is a method, not a pose."
    description="The Independent Observer is being developed as a serious home for cross-disciplinary research, documentary work, and public explanation."
  />
  <section class="section section-white">
    <div class="shell page-grid">
      <aside class="page-aside">Mission</aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Look past the approved frame.</h2>
        <p>
          Public controversies are often presented as isolated disputes between personalities or
          parties. This project instead asks how rules, incentives, historical memory, technology,
          and institutional structure shape the available choices.
        </p>
        <p>
          “Independent” does not mean free from values, error, or perspective. It means the work
          should not conceal its reasoning behind tribal loyalty. Claims should be sourced,
          interpretations should be identifiable, and uncertainty should remain visible.
        </p>
        <div class="principles">
          <div class="principle">
            <span>01</span><div>
              <h3>Evidence before certainty</h3><p>
                Confidence should be proportional to the quality and completeness of the record.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span>02</span><div>
              <h3>Systems before personalities</h3><p>
                Individual conduct matters, but durable incentives and procedures often matter more.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span>03</span><div>
              <h3>Context before outrage</h3><p>
                Historical and institutional context should clarify an issue before rhetoric narrows
                it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span>04</span><div>
              <h3>Correction without ceremony</h3><p>
                Material errors should be acknowledged and corrected clearly when identified.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
